  "body": {
    "id": "thm:no-cross-branch-bounded-chi-square",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Fix \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1/2)\\) and \\(C_{\\mathrm{env}}\\), and suppose \\(\\delta_n/s_n\\to\\infty\\).  For each \\(n\\), let \\(\\Pi_{G,n}\\) and \\(\\Pi_{N,n}\\) be arbitrary priors supported respectively on \\(\\mathcal G_n\\) and \\(\\mathcal N_n(\\delta_n)\\).  Suppose one deterministic supplied pair \\((\\widehat g,\\widehat q)\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal H_n(P)\\) for every law in the union of the two supports, and define the projected-experiment mixtures\n\\[\n \\overline Q_{G,n}=\\int Q_P\\,d\\Pi_{G,n}(P),\n \\qquad\n \\overline Q_{N,n}=\\int Q_P\\,d\\Pi_{N,n}(P).\n\\]\nThen \\(p_{\\mathrm{sel},n}=o(1)\\), and, for all sufficiently large \\(n\\),\n\\[\n \\|\\overline Q_{N,n}-\\overline Q_{G,n}\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}}\n \\ge1-2p_{\\mathrm{sel},n},\n\\]\n\\[\n \\min\\left\\{\n \\chi^2(\\overline Q_{N,n},\\overline Q_{G,n}),\n \\chi^2(\\overline Q_{G,n},\\overline Q_{N,n})\n \\right\\}\n \\ge \\frac{(1-p_{\\mathrm{sel},n})^2}{p_{\\mathrm{sel},n}}-1\n \\longrightarrow\\infty.\n\\]\nConsequently, in the regime \\(\\delta_n/s_n\\to\\infty\\), no Rademacher-partition exponential-Hermite construction, nor any other construction with the stated branch support and common supplied fits, can have uniformly bounded chi-square distance between its Gaussian and non-Gaussian projected mixtures.  Thus the conjunctive construction question has a negative answer.  This result makes no claim about existence of such a pair when \\(\\delta_n\\lesssim s_n\\).",
